; SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
; INTENT.contractile — Purpose and scope for standards
; Helps LLM/SLM agents understand what this repo IS and IS NOT.
;
; Part of the contractile family: MUST, TRUST, DUST, INTENT, ADJUST

; ── Definitions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; INTENT (noun)
;   The purpose contractile. Defines what this repository IS, what it is
;   NOT (anti-purpose), and which architectural decisions are load-bearing.
;   Without INTENT, LLMs drift into scope creep, reverse key decisions,
;   or add features that belong in a different repo.
;
; Scope:
;   INTENT governs the conceptual boundaries of the project — its reason
;   for existing, its domain, and its relationship to the ecosystem.
;   It does NOT specify implementation details (that's MUST and code).
;
; Relationship to other contractiles:
;   - MUST: INTENT explains WHY certain MUSTs exist. If you don't
;     understand a MUST, read INTENT first.
;   - TRUST: The "ask-before-touching" section in INTENT maps directly
;     to TRUST.trust-deny for the most sensitive areas.
;   - ADJUST: INTENT's anti-purpose should include "this software is
;     NOT only for users with perfect vision/hearing/mobility."
;   - DUST: When INTENT changes (repo pivots), related DUST entries
;     should be created for the abandoned direction.
;
; ── End Definitions ──────────────────────────────────────────────

(intent-contractile
  (version "1.0.1")
  (repo "standards")

  ; === Purpose (what this repo IS) ===
  (purpose
    "The canonical source of organization-wide standards, specifications, and governance
     templates for the Hyperpolymath ecosystem. It defines the contractile family
     (MUST/TRUST/DUST/INTENT/ADJUST), the CRG readiness grading system, the RSR
     (Rhodium Standard Repository) requirements, the K9 validation tier model
     (Kennel/Yard/Hunt), the Testing and Benchmarking Taxonomy, the A2ML and K9
     specification languages, and all associated template sets that other repos copy
     as their starting compliance baseline."
  )

  ; === Anti-Purpose (what this repo is NOT — prevents scope creep) ===
  (anti-purpose
    "This repo is NOT a library to import or a framework to depend on at runtime.
     It is NOT a monorepo for implementations — implementations live in their own repos
     and reference standards/ as documentation, not as a build dependency.
     It does NOT contain application code, game logic, or service implementations.
     It does NOT make decisions on behalf of other repos — it defines the criteria
     by which those repos make their own decisions.
     It is NOT the place for per-project CLAUDE.md, STATE, or META files — those
     belong in each repo's .machine_readable/ directory."
  )

  ; === Key Architectural Decisions That Must Not Be Reversed ===
  (architectural-invariants
    ("Contractile family defines five roles: MUST (invariants), TRUST (permissions),
      DUST (rollback/deprecation), INTENT (purpose/scope), ADJUST (accessibility).
      These names and their semantics are stable across the estate.")
    ("K9 validation has three tiers: Kennel (read-only data), Yard (validated writes),
      Hunt (full automation). Tier boundaries must not be blurred.")
    ("CRG v2.0 is deliberately strict: grade D requires RSR compliance + passing tests;
      grade C requires deep annotation; grade B requires 6 diverse external targets;
      publication requires B+. Grades must not be inflated.")
    ("A2ML is the canonical format for machine-readable files in .machine_readable/.
      SCM files are legacy; all new files use A2ML. Migration ongoing.")
    ("contractile.just is always auto-generated via 'contractile gen-just --dir contractiles'.
      Never edit it by hand — edit the source A2ML files and regenerate.")
    ("Template residue is a bug: any {{PLACEHOLDER}} left in a template that reaches
      a real repo is a defect to be fixed, not ignored.")
  )

  ; === Sensitive Areas (if in doubt, ask) ===
  (ask-before-touching
    "1-formats/contractiles/ — changes here propagate to every repo that has copied the templates"
    "4-readiness/component-readiness-grades/ — CRG grade semantics are intentionally stable"
    "rhodium-standard-repositories/ — RSR requirements affect all 500+ estate repos"
    ".machine_readable/ — format is specified; do not add files outside the contractile schema"
    "a2ml/ — specification language; backwards-incompatible changes need an ADR"
    "1-formats/k9/ and 2-protocols/k9-coordination/ — K9 trust tier boundaries are load-bearing"
  )

  ; === Ecosystem Position ===
  (ecosystem
    (belongs-to "standalone — standards is its own top-level repo, not a monorepo subdirectory")
    (depended-on-by
      ("all hyperpolymath repos" "copy 1-formats/contractiles/ templates as compliance baseline")
      ("gitbot-fleet" "reads RSR requirements to automate compliance checks")
      ("hypatia" "references CRG, RSR, and contractile specs for CI rule definitions")
      ("rsr-template-repo" "is the materialised form of RSR requirements defined here"))
  )
)
